@facemorph/stylegan-js bundles no third-party packages. Its emitted JavaScript has no runtime dependencies; the parts
noted as ported in the sources come from FaceMorph's own earlier application, under this package's licence.

ONNX Runtime Web (MIT, Microsoft) is not part of this package. The ORT routes import the runtime from bytes the
caller supplies (normally verified by @facemorph/browser-model-manager from a model manifest), so its licence travels
with those bytes. Model weights are not part of this package either; their usage and redistribution terms are recorded
per model in the docs.

The seed and text inputs use NumPy's legacy RandomState generator (MT19937 with the polar Gaussian), reimplemented in
src/engine/identity.ts so a seed gives the same face as NumPy. It is not recorded whether that implementation was
translated from NumPy or from the reference mt19937ar.c, so both notices are reproduced here.

